{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And Elohim went up from him in the place where He spoke with him.</b> Rashi explained: 'I do not know what this comes to teach us.' And it appears to me that it comes to teach us that the Patriarchs are themselves the chariot, and that the Temple below is aligned opposite the Temple above, as is known — for Jacob was now in Beth El and Luz, and there is the gate of heaven, for these two places were joined with Mount Moriah as explained above in the portion of וַיֵּצֵא (Genesis 28:17). And had it not been stated 'in the place where He spoke with him,' I would say that the Shekhinah went to another place and from there ascended to its dwelling. Therefore it was necessary to specify that Elohim went up directly from this place — so that forever Jacob is below and the Shekhinah is above, and it ascended to its dwelling, to the Temple above, which is aligned opposite the place where He spoke with him in the Temple below."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:32:03.152488516Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}